- content_for :title, "Turniput - Baldrick Board Integration Software"

.max-w-6xl.mx-auto.px-4.sm:px-6.lg:px-8.py-8
  / Breadcrumb
  = render 'shared/breadcrumbs', breadcrumbs: [{ title: 'Home', path: '/' }, { title: 'Baldrick Breakthroughs', path: '/breakthroughs' }, { title: 'Turniput', path: nil }]

  / Main Content Card
  .bg-white.rounded-lg.shadow-lg.overflow-hidden
    / Header Section
    = render 'shared/page_header', title: 'Turniput', subtitle: 'Making lightshow interactivity as simple as pressing a button', image_url: 'big-red-button.png'

    / Content Section
    .px-8.py-8
      .max-w-4xl.mx-auto
        .prose.max-w-none
          / Navigation
          .bg-gray-50.rounded-lg.p-6.mb-8.border.border-gray-200
            h3.text-xl.font-semibold.text-gray-900.mb-4 Quick Navigation
            .grid.md:grid-cols-2.lg:grid-cols-3.gap-4.mb-4
              a.text-indigo-600.hover:text-indigo-800.font-medium href="#what-is-turniput" What is a Turniput
              a.text-indigo-600.hover:text-indigo-800.font-medium href="#input-types" What can I use to Input with a Turniput
              a.text-indigo-600.hover:text-indigo-800.font-medium href="#lamp-control" Turniput Lamp Control
            .border-t.border-gray-300.pt-4
              h4.text-lg.font-semibold.text-gray-700.mb-3 Integrations
              .grid.md:grid-cols-2.gap-4
                a.text-indigo-600.hover:text-indigo-800.font-medium href="#fpp-integration" FPP Integration
                a.text-indigo-600.hover:text-indigo-800.font-medium href="#webhook-integration" Web Hook Integration

          / What is a Turniput
          section#what-is-turniput.mb-12
            h2.text-3xl.font-bold.text-gray-900.mb-6 What is a Turniput
            
            / Introduction
            .mb-8
              p.text-lg.text-gray-700.mb-6
                | From the very beginning, we wanted to make adding interactivity as simple as point and click.
              
              p.text-lg.text-gray-700.mb-6
                | That's why the 
                = link_to "Baldrick8", board_path('baldrick8'), class: "text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 font-medium"
                |  shipped with three inputs that could control not only other Baldrick boards, but also software like FPP.
              
              p.text-lg.text-gray-700.mb-6
                | We've seen people connect them to beam breaks and motion sensors, but by far the most popular use has been with buttons. Pretty quickly, the requests rolled in for a way to control the button lamp too — for example, turning it off when the button couldn't be pressed.
              
              p.text-lg.text-gray-700.mb-6
                | That led us to create the 
                = link_to "BaldrickInput1", board_path('baldrickinput1'), class: "text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-800 font-medium"
                | , a standalone controller dedicated to interactivity, with lamp control built in and improved Turnip Network integration.
              
              p.text-lg.text-gray-700.mb-6
                | And from there, an Input fully powered by the Turnip Network was born: the 
                strong Turniput
                | .
              
              p.text-lg.text-gray-700.mb-8
                | Now standard across all new boards the Turniput allows easy interaction without any scripting or code.

          / What can I use to Input with a Turniput
